Here is an exhaustive, well-organized reference list of multimodal breast cancer datasets used in published research, separated into public and private/restricted.

🟢 PART 1 — PUBLIC DATASETS (Freely Accessible)
Dual-Modality Imaging: Ultrasound + Mammogram
1. BCDR — Breast Cancer Digital Repository
Modalities: Mammogram (film + digital) + Ultrasound + Clinical data + BI-RADS Patients: 1,734 Origin: Portugal (University of Porto / Centro Hospitalar São João) Format: TIFF, CSV Access: Free download for registered users at https://bcdr.eu 
Kaggle
 How to access: Register at https://bcdr.eu → request download of BCDR-FM, BCDR-DM benchmarking sets Why relevant: It contains cases from 1,734 patients with both mammography and ultrasound images, clinical history, lesion segmentation, and image-based descriptors — all BI-RADS classified and annotated by specialized radiologists. 
The Cancer Imaging Archive

2. BCMID — Breast Cancer Multimodal Imaging Dataset
Modalities: Mammogram + Ultrasound (paired per patient) + BI-RADS Patients: 323 Origin: Egypt (Arab Academy for Science, Technology & Maritime Transport / Ayady Almostakbal Hospital, Alexandria) Format: Folders with US and mammogram subfolders per patient + labels CSV Access: Restricted files — register and request at https://zenodo.org/records/14970848 | DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.14970848 Note: The BCMID is the first multimodal dataset from Egypt's breast cancer characterization, providing ultrasound and mammogram images for each patient along with BiRads categories. 
PubMed Central
 Files are restricted; contact authors Noha Tawfik or Noha Ghatwary at the Arab Academy directly.

MRI-Centric Multimodal Datasets
3. Duke Breast Cancer MRI (Duke-Breast-Cancer-MRI)
Modalities: DCE-MRI + Mammogram features (tabular) + Ultrasound features (tabular) + Clinical + Pathology + Genomics Patients: 922 biopsy-confirmed invasive breast cancer cases Origin: Duke University Medical Center, USA Format: DICOM (MRI), CSV (clinical + radiomics features) Access: Freely available via TCIA: https://www.cancerimagingarchive.net/collection/duke-breast-cancer-mri/ DOI: 10.7937/TCIA.e3sv-re93 Why relevant: Clinical data includes mammography characteristics from the preoperative mammogram report and ultrasound features from the preoperative ultrasound report, along with 529 computer-extracted imaging features, demographic, pathology, treatment, outcomes, and genomic data. 
PubMed Central

4. I-SPY1 (ACRIN 6657)
Modalities: DCE-MRI + DWI + Clinical metadata + Pathology response Patients: ~234 (level 2b cohort) Origin: Multi-center USA clinical trial Format: DICOM, CSV Access: Free via TCIA: https://www.cancerimagingarchive.net/collection/ispy1/ How to access: Create a free TCIA account → direct download via NBIA Data Retriever

5. I-SPY2 (ACRIN 6698 / ISPY2)
Modalities: DCE-MRI + DWI + Clinical + Pathologic complete response (pCR) labels Patients: 985 patients total (719 in this collection + 266 in the ACRIN-6698 collection) enrolled from 2010–2016, randomized to one of nine experimental drug arms or control arm. 
Bcdr
 Access: Free via TCIA: https://www.cancerimagingarchive.net/collection/ispy2/ DOI: 10.7937/TCIA.D8Z0-9T85

6. MAMA-MIA
Modalities: DCE-MRI (pre-treatment) + harmonized clinical/demographic variables (49 variables) from 4 TCIA collections Patients: 1,506 multicenter Origin: Aggregated from I-SPY1, I-SPY2, NACT-Pilot, Duke (all TCIA) Access: Free via Zenodo and TCIA: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10565491 Why relevant: The dataset integrates imaging data from four TCIA collections and includes expert annotations of primary tumors and non-mass-enhanced regions, along with 49 harmonized clinical and demographic variables, created with input from 16 breast cancer experts. 
Zenodo

Mammogram-Centric Multimodal Datasets
7. CBIS-DDSM — Curated Breast Imaging Subset of DDSM
Modalities: Film mammogram (scanned) + Pathology labels + Lesion segmentation Patients: 2,620 studies Origin: USA national screening program Format: DICOM Access: Free via TCIA: https://www.cancerimagingarchive.net/collection/cbis-ddsm/ How to access: No registration needed — direct download via NBIA Data Retriever or AWS

8. CDD-CESM — Contrast Enhanced Spectral Mammography Dataset
Modalities: Dual-energy mammogram (low energy + subtracted CESM images) + medical reports + segmentation annotations Patients: 326 patients, 2,006 images Origin: Egypt (National Cancer Institute, Cairo University) Format: JPEG + Excel annotations + DOCX reports Access: Free via TCIA: https://www.cancerimagingarchive.net/collection/cdd-cesm/ DOI: 10.7937/29kw-ae92 Why relevant: The CDD-CESM dataset includes two image types per exam (low energy and subtracted CESM), full medical reports, and manual segmentation annotation for abnormal findings — enabling dual-modality fusion within the mammogram imaging pathway itself. 
