Synthesized research gaps into six novel, feasible deep learning problem statements
Synthesized research gaps into six novel, feasible deep learning problem statements

















Here are 6 deeply reasoned, novel, publishable problem statements for an advanced DL researcher, each grounded strictly in the consolidated research gaps from our full literature review.

🧠 Problem Statement 1
Uncertainty-Aware Missing-Modality Robust Fusion of Ultrasound and Mammogram for Breast Cancer Diagnosis
📌 Gap Addressed
Real-world breast cancer datasets often contain missing information — patient records may lack certain imaging types such as mammograms or histopathology slides — yet most multimodal models discard incomplete cases or use imputation, both of which introduce bias. 
PubMed Central
 No existing US+mammogram fusion model gracefully degrades when one modality is unavailable at inference time.

🎯 Problem Statement
Design an evidential deep learning-based multimodal fusion network for breast cancer diagnosis that dynamically re-weights modality contributions based on per-modality uncertainty, remaining clinically useful even when either ultrasound or mammogram is unavailable at test time.

➡️ Input
Full case: Paired Ultrasound image + Mammogram image (per patient)
Partial case (simulated/real): Only US — OR — Only Mammogram
Auxiliary: BI-RADS category label (available in BCMID)
⬅️ Output
Binary malignancy classification (benign / malignant)
BI-RADS category score (1–5)
Per-modality epistemic uncertainty map (what the model does not know)
Fusion confidence score — how much each modality contributed to the final decision
Grad-CAM overlays per modality for radiologist interpretability
🏗️ Proposed Architecture
Dual-branch encoder (ResNet50 / EfficientNetV2 per modality)
Evidential Deep Learning (EDL) head per branch — outputs Dirichlet distribution parameters instead of softmax probabilities
Dynamic gating module that zeros or down-weights the branch with high uncertainty
Shared cross-modal attention layer for complementary feature alignment
Multi-task decoder: classification head + BI-RADS regression head
📂 Datasets
BCMID (323 patients, paired US + mammogram, BI-RADS labels) — simulate missing modality by random masking
BCDR (1,734 patients, paired US + mammogram) — external validation
BUSI (800 images) — US-only auxiliary training
📊 Evaluation Metrics
AUC, F1, Sensitivity, Specificity, Expected Calibration Error (ECE), performance under 0%, 25%, 50%, 75% missing rate

✅ Why It's Doable
Missing modality simulation is straightforward; BCMID and BCDR have the exact paired data needed; EDL is a well-established framework; no new data collection required.

🧠 Problem Statement 2
