Based on a review of 50 articles from 2019 to 2025, overfitting caused by the scarcity of breast cancer data is a core challenge, while multi-modal fusion becomes even more constrained when combining multiple modalities. 
Nature
 All 35 papers in our literature survey train on centralized datasets — none address the fundamental clinical reality that different hospitals own different modalities (hospital A has US only, hospital B has mammogram only, hospital C has both), and patient data cannot leave its institution due to privacy regulations (HIPAA, GDPR).

