Here are 4 precisely engineered, architecturally novel problem statements — each designed specifically around BCMID's exact structure (323 patients, paired US+Mammogram, image-level BI-RADS labels only, no pixel masks), exploiting the most advanced current DL paradigms.

🔬 FIRST — Understanding BCMID's Exact Constraints
(These constraints directly motivate every design choice below)

BCMID Property	Value	DL Implication
Patients	323	Too small for supervised-only DL → SSL essential
Supervision	BI-RADS label per patient only	No pixel masks → weakly supervised required
Structure	Paired US + Mammo per patient	Patient identity = free supervision signal
Imaging physics	US (acoustic) vs Mammo (X-ray)	Fundamental modality gap → disentanglement needed
BI-RADS scale	1–5 ordinal	Ordinal constraint exploitable
🧠 Problem Statement 1
Cross-Modal Masked Autoencoder (CroMAE): Self-Supervised Pretraining via Asymmetric Cross-Modal Patch Reconstruction for Breast Cancer Diagnosis
📌 Core Research Gap
BCMID has only 323 labeled patients — far too few for supervised deep learning to converge reliably. Existing SSL methods (MAE, SimCLR) work within a single modality. Self-supervised pre-training with masked autoencoding is particularly powerful for small medical datasets because it allows models to learn rich visual representations from unlabeled data before fine-tuning on limited labeled samples. 
ScienceDirect
 However, no existing work exploits cross-modal patient pairing — where the US image of patient P can supervise reconstruction of the masked mammogram of the same patient P — as a free self-supervised signal. This patient-paired cross-modal structure in BCMID is entirely unexploited.

🎯 Problem Statement
Design a Cross-Modal Masked Autoencoder (CroMAE) that — without using any BI-RADS labels — pretrains a shared Vision Transformer by learning to reconstruct heavily masked patches of one modality (US) conditioned on the full unmasked image of the other modality (Mammogram) for the same patient, and vice versa. The pretrained encoder is then fine-tuned with BI-RADS labels using only 10% of labeled patients.

➡️ Precise Input (with exact example)
Stage 1 — Pretraining (No labels used):

Patient P_042:
  US image:    I_us  ∈ ℝ^{1×224×224}   (grayscale, resized)
  Mammo image: I_mm  ∈ ℝ^{1×224×224}   (grayscale, resized)

Step 1: Patchify both images into 16×16 patches
  I_us  → 196 patches of shape 16×16 each
  I_mm  → 196 patches of shape 16×16 each

Step 2: Asymmetric masking
  Mask 75% of I_us patches randomly → 147 patches masked, 49 visible
  I_mm remains fully visible (unmasked) → serves as cross-modal context

Step 3: Encoder input
  Visible US patches (49) + Full Mammo patches (196) 
  → ViT encoder processes concatenated tokens with modality-type embeddings
     [us_token_1, ..., us_token_49, mm_token_1, ..., mm_token_196]
  → Each token has positional embedding + modality embedding (0 for US, 1 for Mammo)
Stage 2 — Fine-tuning (With labels):

Patient P_042:
  I_us  ∈ ℝ^{1×224×224}
  I_mm  ∈ ℝ^{1×224×224}
  y     = BI-RADS category ∈ {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}
  
Using only 32 patients (10% of 323) for fine-tuning
⬅️ Precise Output
Stage 1 — Pretraining output:

Reconstructed masked US patches:
  Î_us_masked ∈ ℝ^{147 × 256}  (147 patches × 16×16 pixels)
  
Reconstruction loss: MSE per pixel of masked patches only
  L_recon = (1/147) Σ ||I_us[masked] - Î_us[masked]||²_F

Symmetric: also reconstruct masked Mammo patches from full US
  → L_recon_total = L_recon(US←Mammo) + L_recon(Mammo←US)
Stage 2 — Fine-tuning output:

Predicted BI-RADS probability vector:
  ŷ ∈ ℝ^5     e.g., [0.03, 0.05, 0.12, 0.71, 0.09]
               → predicted: BI-RADS 4 (malignancy risk: HIGH)

Cross-modal attention map (interpretability):
  A ∈ ℝ^{196×196}   (US patch-to-Mammo patch attention weights)
  → Visualized as heatmap showing which Mammo regions inform which US regions
🏗️ Architecture — CroMAE
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  STAGE 1: CROSS-MODAL MASKED AUTOENCODER PRETRAINING        │
│                                                             │
│  I_us (masked 75%)  I_mm (full)                             │
│       ↓                  ↓                                  │
│  PatchEmbed(16)     PatchEmbed(16)                          │
│  + PosEmb + ModEmb(0)  + PosEmb + ModEmb(1)                 │
│       └──────────┬───────┘                                  │
│           ViT-Base Encoder                                  │
│        (12 layers, 768-dim, shared weights)                 │
│                  ↓                                          │
│         [CLS token, 49 US tokens, 196 MM tokens]            │
│                  ↓                                          │
│     Lightweight MAE Decoder (4 layers, 512-dim)             │
│                  ↓                                          │
│     Reconstruct 147 masked US patches                       │
│     L_recon = MSE(masked patches only)                      │
│                                                             │
│  [Same in reverse: mask Mammo, context=full US]             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                          ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  STAGE 2: WEAKLY SUPERVISED FINE-TUNING                     │
