Novel design choices:

Cross-modal masking: mask one modality, reconstruct from paired other — never done for US+Mammogram
Asymmetric masking ratio: 75% US (high redundancy), 50% Mammo (different density) — informed by information density difference
Modality-type embedding: explicit 0/1 token distinguishes US from Mammo patches in same ViT
Ordinal loss at fine-tuning: BI-RADS is ordinal, not categorical — violating this hurts calibration
