🧠 Problem Statement 2
Ordinal-Constrained Cross-Modal Vision Transformer with Weakly Supervised Lesion Co-Localization from BI-RADS Labels Only
📌 Core Research Gap
BCMID provides only image-level BI-RADS labels — no bounding boxes, no pixel masks. Yet radiologists need to know where in the image the suspicious region is, not just whether cancer exists. All existing weakly supervised localization methods (Grad-CAM, CAM, DINO self-attention) work within a single modality. The critical unmet challenge is: can a model jointly localize the lesion in BOTH the ultrasound AND the mammogram simultaneously, using only the patient-level BI-RADS label? Furthermore, BI-RADS is ordinal (1 < 2 < 3 < 4 < 5) — but all existing work treats it as categorical, discarding the clinical ordering information.

🎯 Problem Statement
Build an Ordinal Cross-Modal Vision Transformer (OrdCMViT) that uses patient-level BI-RADS labels as the only supervision to simultaneously (1) predict BI-RADS grade with ordinal constraint, (2) generate weakly supervised lesion localization maps on US images, and (3) generate co-localization maps on Mammogram images, via cross-modal attention rollout — without any pixel-level annotation.

➡️ Precise Input
Patient P_107 from BCMID:
  US image:      I_us  ∈ ℝ^{1×256×256}
  Mammo image:   I_mm  ∈ ℝ^{1×256×256}
  BI-RADS label: y = 4   (suspicious — one integer label per patient)

Patchification:
  I_us  → N_us = 256 patches (patch_size=16, stride=16)
  I_mm  → N_mm = 256 patches
  Each patch → 768-dim token via linear projection + positional embedding

Modality tokens:
  US stream:    [CLS_us, p_us^1, ..., p_us^256]   shape: 257 × 768
  Mammo stream: [CLS_mm, p_mm^1, ..., p_mm^256]   shape: 257 × 768
⬅️ Precise Output
Output 1 — BI-RADS Classification:

ŷ_ord ∈ ℝ^4  (4 binary outputs for ordinal encoding)
  e.g., [σ(f1)=0.98, σ(f2)=0.91, σ(f3)=0.82, σ(f4)=0.14]
  → Decoded BI-RADS grade = 4  (first k where σ(fk) < 0.5)
  → Confidence: 82% probability lesion is ≥ BI-RADS 3 (actionable)
Output 2 — Weakly Supervised US Lesion Map:

CAM_us ∈ ℝ^{16×16}  (upsampled to 256×256)
  e.g., peak activation at pixel coordinates (128, 145)
  → Lesion centroid estimated: (128, 145) in US space
  → Heatmap overlay: warm = high malignancy relevance
Output 3 — Co-Localization Map on Mammogram:

CAM_mm ∈ ℝ^{16×16}  (upsampled to 256×256)
  → Derived via cross-modal attention: which Mammo patches 
    attended most to the high-activation US patches?
  → Lesion centroid estimated in Mammo space: (110, 198)
  
Cross-modal consistency score:
  S_consistency = cosine_sim(CAM_us_features, CAM_mm_features)
  e.g., S_consistency = 0.87  (high = same lesion found in both)
🏗️ Architecture — OrdCMViT
I_us → PatchEmbed → US token stream [CLS_us, p¹...p²⁵⁶]
I_mm → PatchEmbed → MM token stream [CLS_mm, p¹...p²⁵⁶]

┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│        DUAL-STREAM CROSS-MODAL TRANSFORMER           │
│                                                      │
│  Layer 1-6: Within-modal self-attention              │
│    US stream:  Multi-head Self-Attention (US only)   │
│    MM stream:  Multi-head Self-Attention (MM only)   │
│                                                      │
│  Layer 7-12: Cross-modal cross-attention             │
│    US patches attend to MM patches (and vice versa): │
│    Q_us = W_Q · h_us,  K_mm = W_K · h_mm            │
│    A_cross = softmax(Q_us · K_mm^T / √d)            │
│    → Each US patch can query relevant Mammo patches  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ↓                    ↓
        CLS_us (768d)        CLS_mm (768d)
              └──────┬─────────┘
               Concat → 1536d → MLP
                          ↓
              Ordinal heads: f₁, f₂, f₃, f₄
              Loss: L_ord = Σₖ BCE(σ(fₖ), 1[y≥k])
                          ↓
               ŷ_ord → BI-RADS prediction

LOCALIZATION (no extra supervision):
  Gradient of L_ord w.r.t. patch tokens → Grad-CAM
  Cross-modal attention rollout A_cross → co-localization
  CAM_us = Σᵢ αᵢ · h_us^i   (weighted by gradients)
  CAM_mm = A_cross^T · CAM_us (propagated to Mammo space)
Novelty:

Cross-modal attention rollout for co-localization — localizing in both modalities from one label
Ordinal BI-RADS loss — first to exploit BI-RADS clinical ordering in multimodal transformer
Cross-modal CAM propagation — Mammo localization derived from US attention map via cross-attention weights (zero extra annotation cost)
📊 Evaluation
