🧠 Problem Statement 3
Patient-Paired Cross-Modal Contrastive Disentanglement Transformer (P²CDT): Separating Modality-Specific Noise from Tumour-Biology Signal for Few-Shot BI-RADS Grading
📌 Core Research Gap
The fundamental challenge in US+Mammogram fusion is the modality gap — ultrasound encodes acoustic reflection (soft tissue contrast, vascularity, lesion echogenicity) while mammography encodes X-ray attenuation (calcification, architectural distortion, density). Existing fusion methods concatenate or average these modalities, mixing their complementary signals with modality-specific noise (speckle in US, radiation artifacts in Mammo). No existing method disentangles the shared tumour-biology latent representation from modality-specific artifacts in the US+Mammogram context. The patient-pairing in BCMID is the unique key: the same tumour biology is simultaneously imaged by both modalities in every patient — this structure should enforce disentanglement without any extra supervision.

🎯 Problem Statement
Develop a Patient-Paired Cross-Modal Contrastive Disentanglement Transformer (P²CDT) that uses the within-patient US-Mammogram pairing as a self-supervised signal to disentangle a shared tumour-biology latent code z_shared (modality-invariant) from modality-specific latent codes z_us and z_mm (modality-specific texture/artifact codes), then perform few-shot BI-RADS grading using only z_shared — with only 20% labeled patients.

➡️ Precise Input
BCMID Patient P_201:
  US image:    I_us  ∈ ℝ^{1×224×224}
  Mammo image: I_mm  ∈ ℝ^{1×224×224}

Encoding (shared ViT backbone, E_θ):
  h_us = E_θ(I_us)  ∈ ℝ^{768}   (CLS token representation)
  h_mm = E_θ(I_mm)  ∈ ℝ^{768}

Disentanglement projection:
  z_shared_us = W_s · h_us  ∈ ℝ^{256}   shared tumour factor from US view
  z_shared_mm = W_s · h_mm  ∈ ℝ^{256}   shared tumour factor from Mammo view
  z_spec_us   = W_u · h_us  ∈ ℝ^{128}   US-specific (speckle, acoustic shadow)
  z_spec_mm   = W_m · h_mm  ∈ ℝ^{128}   Mammo-specific (calcification texture)

Contrastive pairs for same patient P_201:
  Positive pair: (z_shared_us^{P201}, z_shared_mm^{P201})   ← same tumour
  Negative pairs: (z_shared_us^{P201}, z_shared_mm^{P_k≠201}) ← different patients
⬅️ Precise Output
Output 1 — Disentangled Latent Codes:

z_shared ∈ ℝ^{256}   → tumour biology embedding (used for classification)
z_spec_us ∈ ℝ^{128}  → US-specific factors (speckle, acoustic, vascularity)
z_spec_mm ∈ ℝ^{128}  → Mammo-specific factors (calcification, density, distortion)

Example for Patient P_201 (BI-RADS 4):
  z_shared = [0.82, -0.31, 0.67, ..., 0.44]   (256 values — tumour semantics)
  z_spec_us = [0.21, 0.09, -0.55, ..., 0.33]  (128 values — US texture noise)
  z_spec_mm = [-0.44, 0.72, ..., 0.18]         (128 values — Mammo calcification)
Output 2 — Few-shot BI-RADS Prediction:

ŷ = MLP(z_shared)  (linear classifier trained on 20% labeled patients = 65 patients)
  → ŷ = [0.04, 0.06, 0.09, 0.72, 0.09]   → BI-RADS 4 (probability: 72%)
Output 3 — Reconstruction (for disentanglement verification):

Î_us = Decoder_us(z_shared ⊕ z_spec_us)  ∈ ℝ^{1×224×224}
Î_mm = Decoder_mm(z_shared ⊕ z_spec_mm) ∈ ℝ^{1×224×224}

Cross-modal generation (novel test):
  Î_us_from_mm = Decoder_us(z_shared_mm ⊕ z_spec_us_mean)
  → Synthetic US image generated from Mammo shared code
  → Measures: does z_shared truly capture cross-modal invariant features?
🏗️ Architecture — P²CDT
I_us, I_mm → Shared ViT-Small Encoder (E_θ)
                    ↓
             h_us, h_mm ∈ ℝ^{768}
                    ↓
    ┌───────────────┼───────────────┐
    ↓               ↓               ↓
  W_s (shared)   W_u (US-spec)  W_m (MM-spec)
    ↓               ↓               ↓
 z_shared_us   z_spec_us       z_shared_mm
 z_shared_mm              + z_spec_mm
    ↓
LOSS 1 — Cross-modal Contrastive (InfoNCE):
  L_contrast = -log exp(sim(z_s_us^P, z_s_mm^P)/τ)
                    ─────────────────────────────────
               Σ_{k≠P} exp(sim(z_s_us^P, z_s_mm^k)/τ)
  (same patient US-Mammo = positive; cross-patient = negative)

LOSS 2 — Orthogonality (disentanglement enforcement):
  L_ortho = ||z_shared_us · z_spec_us^T||_F
           + ||z_shared_mm · z_spec_mm^T||_F
  (shared and specific codes must be orthogonal = uncorrelated)

LOSS 3 — Reconstruction:
  L_recon = ||I_us - Decoder_us(z_shared⊕z_spec_us)||²
           + ||I_mm - Decoder_mm(z_shared⊕z_spec_mm)||²

LOSS 4 — Cross-Reconstruction (key novelty):
  L_cross = ||I_us - Decoder_us(z_shared_mm⊕z_spec_us_mean)||²
  (Mammo's shared code should reconstruct realistic US appearance)

TOTAL UNSUPERVISED LOSS:
  L_SSL = L_contrast + λ₁L_ortho + λ₂L_recon + λ₃L_cross

SUPERVISED (20% labels only):
  L_cls = CE(MLP(z_shared), y_birads)
  L_total = L_SSL + λ₄L_cls
Novelty:

Cross-reconstruction loss forces z_shared to be truly modality-invariant (not just aligned)
Patient pairing as contrastive supervision — zero-cost labeling signal
Orthogonality constraint mathematically guarantees disentanglement
z_spec interpretation — first method to explicitly characterize what makes US different from Mammo in the same patient
