PART 1 — Validating Localization Without Ground Truth
The Core Problem
BCMID has zero pixel-level annotations — no bounding boxes, no masks. Yet you claim the model localizes lesions. How do you prove it?

The answer: Proxy Validation via Transfer (standard in weakly supervised literature)
You never evaluate localization ON BCMID. Instead you use external datasets that DO have pixel masks, as a zero-shot proxy test — the model trained on BCMID is evaluated for localization quality on an external set where ground truth masks exist.

Strategy 1 — Pointing Game on External US Dataset (BUSI)
Train:    BCMID (US + Mammogram, BI-RADS labels only)
Test:     BUSI  (Ultrasound only, with ground truth lesion MASKS)

Metric:   Pointing Game Accuracy (PGA)
          PGA = 1 if argmax(CAM) falls INSIDE ground truth mask
                0 if argmax(CAM) falls OUTSIDE mask
          
          Report: PGA across all BUSI test cases
          
Interpretation:
  If PGA >> random baseline (random point inside 224×224 = ~10-30% 
  depending on lesion size), the model has learned to localize lesions
  even without pixel supervision.
Strategy 2 — IoU @ Threshold on External Mammogram Dataset (CBIS-DDSM)
Train:    BCMID (paired US + Mammo, BI-RADS)
Test:     CBIS-DDSM (mammogram with expert ROI annotations)

Method:   Threshold CAM at 50% of max activation → binary mask
          Compute IoU (Intersection over Union) vs. expert ROI

Metric:   IoU@0.1, IoU@0.3, IoU@0.5
          (IoU@0.1 = very lenient, IoU@0.5 = strict)
          
WHY valid: You're testing TRANSFER of localization — the model learned
           "what a suspicious lesion looks like" from BI-RADS labels on BCMID
           and we verify this generalizes to an annotated dataset.
Strategy 3 — Energy in Lesion Region (No Masks, Sanity Check)
Even without external datasets, you can do a self-consistency test on BCMID:

Hypothesis: Higher BI-RADS patients should have more concentrated CAM energy

Test:
  Compute CAM entropy per patient:
    H_i = -Σ_p cam(p) * log(cam(p))   (uniform = high entropy, focused = low entropy)
  
  Correlation: Spearman(BI-RADS_label, -H_i)
  
  Expected: High BI-RADS → lower CAM entropy (model more focused on specific region)
  
  This doesn't prove the location is correct, but proves the model
  is more discriminative (less diffuse) for higher-grade lesions.
Strategy 4 — Radiologist Likert Study (Gold Standard for Clinical Work)
For N=20 test patients (from BCMID visualization outputs):
  Show radiologist: original US + CAM overlay
  Ask: "Does the highlighted region correspond to 
        where you would look for a suspicious lesion?"
  Scale: 1 (Not at all) to 5 (Exactly)
  
Report: Mean ± SD Likert score per BI-RADS category
